        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "214e8562-60a9-5551-9d76-fe808f28972f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Red Coffee, Clarence Nash\n- Characters: Little Quacker, Donald Duck, Daisy Duck\n- Places: Watonga, Oklahoma\n\nFacts:\n- Clarence Nash was born on December 7, 1904, in the rural community of Watonga, Oklahoma.\n- Clarence Nash was an American voice actor.\n- In 1940, Clarence Nash was also known as the voice of Daisy Duck.\n- Clarence Nash provided the distinctive voice of Disney's Donald Duck for 50 years.\n- A street in Watonga, Oklahoma, is named in honor of Clarence Nash.\n- Clarence Nash died on February 20, 1985.\n- In Little Quacker, Red Coffee uncreditedly supplied a line by Tom.\n- Red Coffee's rendition of Little Quacker's voice was mostly an impersonation of Donald Duck as performed by Clarence Nash.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "3ee2e335-ddd0-524c-9204-ad8771dba9e7",
        "text": "Page: Little Quacker. Sentence: line by Tom, was supplied by (uncredited) Red Coffee; Coffee's rendition of Quacker's voice was mostly an impersonation of Disney's Donald Duck as performed by Clarence Nash.\nPage: Clarence Nash. Sentence: Clarence Charles \"Ducky\" Nash (December 7, 1904 – February 20, 1985) was an American voice actor.\nPage: Clarence Nash. Sentence: He is best known for the Disney cartoon character Donald Duck, whose distinctive voice he provided for 50 years, also known as the voice of Daisy Duck in 1940.\nPage: Clarence Nash. Sentence: He was born in the rural community of Watonga, Oklahoma, and a street in that town is named in his honor.",
